1
00:00:25,154 --> 00:00:27,471
I'm not a special person,

2
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:31,011
but I'm not a special person.

3
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:35,934
The sun is a light, and I'm
always looking forward to it.

4
00:00:36,874 --> 00:00:42,194
I'm not a little bit of a
light, but I'm not a light.

5
00:00:43,134 --> 00:00:46,851
I'm not a light, but I'm not a light.

6
00:00:46,934 --> 00:00:52,454
I'm not a light, but I'm not a light.

7
00:01:32,714 --> 00:01:34,514
It's all coming together.

8
00:01:34,994 --> 00:01:37,191
Tachimana's charm skill has proven useful.

9
00:01:37,274 --> 00:01:38,921
I barely had to do anything.

10
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:43,111
So what exactly did you do to her?

11
00:01:43,194 --> 00:01:45,311
I boosted the power of her charm skill.

12
00:01:45,394 --> 00:01:49,431
Just enough to make it go a bit haywire,
which so happened to weaken the hero.

13
00:01:49,514 --> 00:01:50,911
Two birds with one stone?

14
00:01:50,994 --> 00:01:53,311
By now, the kingdom should
be utterly overwhelmed?

15
00:01:53,394 --> 00:01:55,411
Trying to quell the riots in the capital,

16
00:01:55,494 --> 00:01:58,711
providing us with the opportunity to
have the humans destroy themselves.

17
00:01:58,794 --> 00:02:00,206
That is totally twisted!

18
00:02:00,354 --> 00:02:01,184
Head made!

19
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,097
Emergency!

20
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:04,731
All communications with the troops
advancing on the capital have been cut off!

21
00:02:04,814 --> 00:02:06,351
Are you saying they were wiped out?

22
00:02:06,434 --> 00:02:10,434
Actually, it would seem they've all
gone back to their normal lives.

23
00:02:10,794 --> 00:02:14,265
Our scouts say they're now
plowing fields completely naked.

24
00:02:14,454 --> 00:02:15,334
Why naked?

25
00:02:15,694 --> 00:02:17,171
That point remains unclear.

26
00:02:17,254 --> 00:02:22,078
However, we can confirm that they've lost
all their memories of the last few days.

27
00:02:22,294 --> 00:02:26,531
How could there be a skill that can instantly
dispel the heroes' charms in hundreds?

28
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:27,555
It's impossible.

29
00:02:27,994 --> 00:02:29,671
I don't get what the big deal is.

30
00:02:29,754 --> 00:02:33,191
What do you think would happen if all
our charmed hostages made an advance on

31
00:02:33,274 --> 00:02:36,731
the enemy only to have their charms
dispelled moments after they've reached them?

32
00:02:36,814 --> 00:02:38,551
Well, it'd make the hostages useless,

33
00:02:38,634 --> 00:02:41,971
which would defeat the whole reason
why we're here in the first place.

34
00:02:42,054 --> 00:02:43,466
Wait, that's really bad!

35
00:02:44,114 --> 00:02:45,654
No, this isn't happening.

36
00:02:45,914 --> 00:02:50,131
All those peeled potatoes, mop floors,
and cobbled shoes can't be for nothing.

37
00:02:50,214 --> 00:02:53,591
It took an entire year working myself
to the bone just to become head maid.

38
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:57,671
All the while patiently gathering information
so I could craft the perfect plan.

39
00:02:57,754 --> 00:02:59,611
And yet somehow I miss
the one human in the

40
00:02:59,694 --> 00:03:01,671
entire kingdom who can undo mind control?

41
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:02,872
Who even does that?

42
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:04,891
This is really bad!

43
00:03:04,974 --> 00:03:06,754
This is really, really sad!

44
00:03:07,094 --> 00:03:08,231
What are you gonna do?

45
00:03:08,314 --> 00:03:09,144
This is really sad!

46
00:03:09,227 --> 00:03:10,391
There's no use fighting it.

47
00:03:10,474 --> 00:03:12,951
We'll abandon the kingdom
falls to charm strategy.

48
00:03:13,034 --> 00:03:15,651
Oh, so does that mean you'll
have some kind of backup plan?

49
00:03:15,734 --> 00:03:16,564
You know what?

50
00:03:16,647 --> 00:03:17,477
Screw it, honestly.

51
00:03:20,314 --> 00:03:22,902
How about we just blow
up the whole kingdom?

52
00:03:25,034 --> 00:03:27,194
Hey, Iki, what is this place?

53
00:03:27,474 --> 00:03:30,811
This chamber is where the kingdom
stores its strongest weapons.

54
00:03:30,894 --> 00:03:31,724
Princess,

55
00:03:31,807 --> 00:03:35,251
as much as I regret that it's come to
this, Due to unforeseen interference,

56
00:03:35,334 --> 00:03:37,511
we've been forced to
abandon our original plan.

57
00:03:37,594 --> 00:03:40,674
The only path left to us
is to use our last resort.

58
00:03:41,234 --> 00:03:42,064
Huh?

59
00:03:42,147 --> 00:03:45,551
You're saying one plan failed and now
we're already down to our last resort?

60
00:03:45,634 --> 00:03:48,411
Sounds like it was a pretty
stupid plan to begin with.

61
00:03:48,494 --> 00:03:52,731
I prefer, Your Highness, to see it as a
sign of how desperate our situation is.

62
00:03:52,814 --> 00:03:57,755
Regardless, I'm not comfortable using the
Kingdom's defenses to achieve my own ends.

63
00:03:57,914 --> 00:04:00,855
Yet you're fine with half
measures, Your Highness.

64
00:04:01,294 --> 00:04:04,294
You've borne the weight of
so much all by yourself.

65
00:04:04,714 --> 00:04:08,934
The power behind that door is yours
to take by right, don't you think?

66
00:04:12,394 --> 00:04:14,954
Remember that suffocating lonely world?

67
00:04:15,454 --> 00:04:17,925
Do you truly miss your life in the castle?

68
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:20,291
But the seal...

69
00:04:20,374 --> 00:04:23,474
It requires two royal family members.

70
00:04:23,694 --> 00:04:25,812
There's no need to worry about that.

71
00:04:28,714 --> 00:04:29,834
Let's not forget.

72
00:04:30,394 --> 00:04:32,688
You've also been touched by the goddess

73
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,894
Come on you too hero, huh? Oh, sorry.

74
00:04:37,154 --> 00:04:38,931
I haven't really been listening

75
00:04:39,014 --> 00:04:41,631
Remember what I said you
wanted to be stronger,

76
00:04:41,714 --> 00:04:45,234
and I told you that I could
teach you a way to do that.

77
00:04:52,274 --> 00:04:56,494
We have what we need so we
can finally defeat Jingle Jee!

78
00:04:57,254 --> 00:04:58,134
Jingle Jee?

79
00:05:05,374 --> 00:05:08,231
Manual manual manual found it.

80
00:05:08,314 --> 00:05:10,631
This doesn't feel right.

81
00:05:10,714 --> 00:05:11,711
Why go so far?

82
00:05:11,794 --> 00:05:14,011
The last thing I want
to do is thread military

83
00:05:14,094 --> 00:05:15,971
action just to make a point to my father.

84
00:05:16,054 --> 00:05:19,591
All this time and you still
need it spelled out for you.

85
00:05:19,674 --> 00:05:25,411
Working for you this last

86
00:05:25,494 --> 00:05:26,991
year has been excruciating.

87
00:05:27,074 --> 00:05:28,771
That's why I'll save.

88
00:05:28,854 --> 00:05:33,501
For every second, I spend turning your
worthless kingdom into a pile of rubble!

89
00:05:34,874 --> 00:05:37,971
Sounds like she's been
holding that back for a while.

90
00:05:38,054 --> 00:05:40,171
Hey, what do you want to
do with the other one?

91
00:05:40,254 --> 00:05:41,084
Oh, the hero?

92
00:05:41,354 --> 00:05:42,883
I've got the perfect idea.

93
00:05:43,174 --> 00:05:45,431
We plug her in and use her as a battery.

94
00:05:45,514 --> 00:05:47,808
She has more than enough goddess power.

95
00:05:48,994 --> 00:05:49,824
Battery...

96
00:05:49,907 --> 00:05:51,474
Wait, are you guys talking about -

97
00:05:53,514 --> 00:05:56,014
Now then, Viz, it's time to wreck havoc!

98
00:05:56,214 --> 00:05:57,254
Switch on!

99
00:06:08,334 --> 00:06:09,574
What's going on?

100
00:06:09,834 --> 00:06:11,716
Jinguuji, what's that over there?

101
00:06:24,894 --> 00:06:26,054
Just stop!

102
00:06:28,994 --> 00:06:29,824
Smash!

103
00:06:30,894 --> 00:06:32,754
Hey, Shen, what is that thing?

104
00:06:33,534 --> 00:06:35,416
Well, it's definitely something.

105
00:06:36,174 --> 00:06:37,974
Now is not the time for jokes.

106
00:06:38,534 --> 00:06:41,491
I get that you're upset, but
no need to bite my head off.

107
00:06:41,574 --> 00:06:42,515
How interesting.

108
00:06:43,114 --> 00:06:45,173
Do you see something, Interrogator?

109
00:06:45,414 --> 00:06:48,174
It's cute. That doesn't help. Oh, sorry.

110
00:06:48,374 --> 00:06:51,731
I meant to say it reminds me of
something I saw in a book long ago.

111
00:06:51,814 --> 00:06:54,873
A creature said to be this
kingdom's guardian deity.

112
00:06:54,974 --> 00:06:55,856
Guardian deity?

113
00:06:56,034 --> 00:06:58,331
You mean those weird forest
animals with the long ears?

114
00:06:58,414 --> 00:07:01,120
big and intimidating,
yet surprisingly cuddly.

115
00:07:01,234 --> 00:07:02,931
And they're fiercely
protective of believers,

116
00:07:03,014 --> 00:07:05,838
and their faces can open
up and shoot out light.

117
00:07:06,334 --> 00:07:10,051
If it's designed after one of those
things, then maybe it showed up to help us.

118
00:07:10,134 --> 00:07:12,671
That's what guardian
deities are supposed to do.

119
00:07:12,754 --> 00:07:15,107
It's possible that this is a lucky omen.

120
00:07:15,994 --> 00:07:17,651
Whoa, thanks, guardian deity.

121
00:07:17,734 --> 00:07:21,322
Actually, based on my experience,
I wouldn't get my hopes up.

122
00:07:34,854 --> 00:07:36,034
Case in point.

123
00:07:36,774 --> 00:07:39,831
Okay, I guess that's a never
mind on the thanks, then.

124
00:07:39,914 --> 00:07:40,794
What is this?

125
00:07:41,114 --> 00:07:44,854
Why would our guardian deity
turn against us? Your majesty?

126
00:07:45,094 --> 00:07:47,329
Can you tell us more about that thing?

127
00:07:47,554 --> 00:07:51,294
It is our kingdom's ancient
defense weapon, Mepon.

128
00:07:51,894 --> 00:07:55,071
A gift bestowed to us by our
goddess in ancient times.

129
00:07:55,154 --> 00:07:57,751
It can mount the enemy's heart
with its adorable design.

130
00:07:57,834 --> 00:08:00,571
and melt fortifications with
its enormous beam weapon.

131
00:08:00,654 --> 00:08:01,484
Isn't it dark?

132
00:08:01,567 --> 00:08:05,178
Of course the goddess would make
something so completely asinine.

133
00:08:05,414 --> 00:08:09,651
But the guardian deity can only be activated
by two members of the royal family,

134
00:08:09,734 --> 00:08:11,263
each bearing a holy crest.

135
00:08:11,354 --> 00:08:12,391
How could this be?

136
00:08:12,474 --> 00:08:13,533
Then it has to be.

137
00:08:14,154 --> 00:08:16,683
Tachibana and the
princess are behind this.

138
00:08:17,234 --> 00:08:18,064
Tachibana.

139
00:08:19,494 --> 00:08:21,774
So, any idea how we take it down?

140
00:08:21,914 --> 00:08:23,571
What makes you think I'd know?

141
00:08:23,654 --> 00:08:24,674
Uh, dang it.

142
00:08:24,994 --> 00:08:27,351
This thing's got a lot
more kick than I thought.

143
00:08:27,434 --> 00:08:29,074
I'm gonna adjust it a bit.

144
00:08:29,214 --> 00:08:31,871
Don't you dare even think
about adjusting anything.

145
00:08:31,954 --> 00:08:35,191
You already missed the first shot and
messing with it will only make things worse.

146
00:08:35,274 --> 00:08:37,921
Quit whining, I'll hit
the next one for sure!

147
00:08:42,434 --> 00:08:43,794
It's powering up again!

148
00:08:44,134 --> 00:08:45,794
Your Majesty, please run!

149
00:08:51,874 --> 00:08:53,992
Jinguji, we need to get out of here!

150
00:08:54,094 --> 00:08:58,800
Schwarz, as an adult, I can tell you we're
nothing if not complicated creatures.

151
00:08:58,894 --> 00:09:00,674
There's a darkness inside us.

152
00:09:00,854 --> 00:09:03,374
It touches everything, even love.

153
00:09:03,534 --> 00:09:06,431
A handsome face really does
make anything sound believable.

154
00:09:06,514 --> 00:09:08,690
I thought Tachibana was no different.

155
00:09:08,774 --> 00:09:10,892
However, I see now that I was wrong.

156
00:09:11,074 --> 00:09:13,351
The robot might look
embarrassingly stupid,

157
00:09:13,434 --> 00:09:17,022
but it is undoubtedly a vicious
and powerful killing machine.

158
00:09:17,754 --> 00:09:20,491
Tachibana would never unleash
something like that on purpose.

159
00:09:20,574 --> 00:09:21,791
So you're worried about him?

160
00:09:21,874 --> 00:09:23,734
It doesn't matter how I feel.

161
00:09:24,054 --> 00:09:29,314
Whoever's controlling the Guardian
deity, it's my responsibility to stop it.

162
00:09:34,094 --> 00:09:38,051
Well, I'm not going to stand here and
let you take all the glory for yourself.

163
00:09:38,134 --> 00:09:38,994
Are you sure?

164
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:44,391
You and I are the only ones in the castle
who can do anything against that robot.

165
00:09:44,474 --> 00:09:47,671
If we don't make a stand here and
now, it'll destroy the whole kingdom.

166
00:09:47,754 --> 00:09:49,166
Isn't that what this is?

167
00:09:50,194 --> 00:09:51,534
It's exactly that.

168
00:09:52,614 --> 00:09:54,496
Well, you can take it from here.

169
00:09:55,354 --> 00:09:56,184
Hm?

170
00:09:56,714 --> 00:10:00,211
Thing is, my supernatural strength
is tied to my proximity to Tachibana,

171
00:10:00,294 --> 00:10:01,234
who isn't here.

172
00:10:01,714 --> 00:10:03,091
So I won't be much help.

173
00:10:03,174 --> 00:10:04,711
Dude, you gotta be kidding me!

174
00:10:04,794 --> 00:10:06,091
You at least have a plan, right?

175
00:10:06,174 --> 00:10:08,871
Something that involves saving
everyone and not leaving me to die?

176
00:10:08,954 --> 00:10:10,211
I'm sorry, but I don't.

177
00:10:10,294 --> 00:10:11,631
What's the matter with you?!

178
00:10:11,714 --> 00:10:14,571
Correct me if I'm wrong, but can't
his sword cut through anything?

179
00:10:14,654 --> 00:10:17,271
So, it stands to reason that it
could also cut through the beam.

180
00:10:17,354 --> 00:10:19,648
That's a good idea, let's go with that.

181
00:10:19,934 --> 00:10:21,511
Can we talk about this first?

182
00:10:21,594 --> 00:10:23,951
A slap-together plan
cannot be our best option!

183
00:10:24,034 --> 00:10:25,991
If you've got a better one, I'm all ears.

184
00:10:26,074 --> 00:10:27,991
We're kinda out of time to brainstorm.

185
00:10:28,074 --> 00:10:29,774
Good luck. Don't die.

186
00:10:31,054 --> 00:10:31,894
No! One!

187
00:10:32,154 --> 00:10:36,507
And remember, we're all counting on
you to make sure we don't end up dead.

188
00:10:38,274 --> 00:10:39,104
This way!

189
00:10:39,187 --> 00:10:40,294
Please remain calm!

190
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:43,874
Take steps!

191
00:11:06,394 --> 00:11:07,531
Would you look at that?

192
00:11:07,614 --> 00:11:08,951
Guess it did work.

193
00:11:09,034 --> 00:11:10,916
Nice you actually did something.

194
00:11:17,014 --> 00:11:20,471
Because if I don't stop it then
You're gonna die, and I'm gonna die,

195
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:22,025
and everyone's gonna die!

196
00:11:22,254 --> 00:11:24,351
You're starting to sound like a real hero.

197
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:25,674
NO ONE ASKED YOU!

198
00:11:29,054 --> 00:11:31,271
Congratulations, humans,
you're all still breathing.

199
00:11:31,354 --> 00:11:32,184
Consider me a rat!

200
00:11:32,267 --> 00:11:33,151
Whose voice is that?

201
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,711
Did it come from inside the Watson?

202
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:36,088
That sounded familiar.

203
00:11:36,854 --> 00:11:39,266
As a reward, I'll share with you my name.

204
00:11:39,694 --> 00:11:44,054
I am this, the incomparably skilled,
top officer for the great demon lord.

205
00:11:44,294 --> 00:11:47,531
And when I'm through with you, I'm gonna
take your corpses as soon as you...

206
00:11:47,614 --> 00:11:48,444
Oh, it's her.

207
00:11:48,527 --> 00:11:52,011
If you're one of the Demon Lord's officers,
then there's no need to hold back.

208
00:11:52,094 --> 00:11:54,351
I'm gonna cut you into tiny little pieces!

209
00:11:54,434 --> 00:11:55,711
Really intimidating, Sparts.

210
00:11:55,794 --> 00:11:56,624
You're doing awesome.

211
00:11:56,707 --> 00:11:58,271
You totally got this, buddy.

212
00:11:58,354 --> 00:11:59,530
Can it, both of you!

213
00:12:00,694 --> 00:12:03,400
You talk a lot for a
glorified side character.

214
00:12:03,574 --> 00:12:06,339
It's gonna be fun watching
you eat those words.

215
00:12:06,474 --> 00:12:07,304
What?

216
00:12:07,387 --> 00:12:09,251
Am I losing it, or can she
hear us from inside that thing?

217
00:12:09,334 --> 00:12:11,031
I'm guessing it's those stupid ears.

218
00:12:11,114 --> 00:12:12,585
What are you waiting for?

219
00:12:12,734 --> 00:12:15,891
It's not like I got your precious
hero in here with me or anything.

220
00:12:15,974 --> 00:12:16,814
Oh, wait.

221
00:12:17,634 --> 00:12:19,634
She's using Tachibana as a shield?

222
00:12:19,874 --> 00:12:21,674
Let him go, you dirty cowards!

223
00:12:22,094 --> 00:12:23,694
Now, let's not be so harsh.

224
00:12:24,094 --> 00:12:26,091
How else could she
level the playing field?

225
00:12:26,174 --> 00:12:27,939
She's just a child, after all.

226
00:12:28,674 --> 00:12:32,071
Such a clever plan, too, did
you come up with it yourself?

227
00:12:32,154 --> 00:12:33,714
Oh, that is it!

228
00:12:34,194 --> 00:12:37,334
Do you want to die,
four-eyes? You're so gorgeous!

229
00:12:39,614 --> 00:12:42,231
Why did you have to go
and provoke her like that?

230
00:12:42,314 --> 00:12:43,144
Good.

231
00:12:43,227 --> 00:12:44,272
Next part's on you.

232
00:12:44,534 --> 00:12:45,634
Get ready. Wait.

233
00:12:51,994 --> 00:12:53,114
That felt good.

234
00:12:58,414 --> 00:13:00,351
Did I vaporize Four Eyes and his friends?

235
00:13:00,434 --> 00:13:01,264
Of course not!

236
00:13:01,354 --> 00:13:02,471
You missed, you idiot!

237
00:13:02,554 --> 00:13:05,231
Now they're getting away because
of your gross incompetence.

238
00:13:05,314 --> 00:13:07,231
Get your act together and keep firing!

239
00:13:07,314 --> 00:13:08,751
You should have kept blasting from the

240
00:13:08,834 --> 00:13:11,311
beginning instead of
trading banter with them.

241
00:13:11,394 --> 00:13:13,031
Mepon isn't built to rapid fire.

242
00:13:13,114 --> 00:13:14,691
It has to cool down for
a while before it can

243
00:13:14,774 --> 00:13:16,731
shoot off another one of
its adorable deathbeds.

244
00:13:16,814 --> 00:13:19,091
I'm sorry if you've been
wasting shots this whole time.

245
00:13:19,174 --> 00:13:20,115
Get off my back.

246
00:13:20,274 --> 00:13:22,151
At least I'm trying to keep
them distracted with witty

247
00:13:22,234 --> 00:13:24,731
conversations so they don't
notice we have a weakness.

248
00:13:24,814 --> 00:13:26,531
But when you say witty conversation?

249
00:13:26,614 --> 00:13:28,391
Are you talking about the part
where you revealed to them?

250
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:29,791
exactly where the hero is?

251
00:13:29,874 --> 00:13:33,371
Did you think that four-eyed barbarian
kept goading you because I was funny?

252
00:13:33,454 --> 00:13:36,551
Quit moaning and stop him before
he's close enough to attack.

253
00:13:36,634 --> 00:13:37,464
Well,

254
00:13:37,547 --> 00:13:39,231
if he's stopped criticizing
me for five seconds

255
00:13:39,314 --> 00:13:42,138
then maybe I can get back
to trying to kill him.

256
00:13:45,374 --> 00:13:46,391
Get ready to land.

257
00:13:46,474 --> 00:13:47,331
This is all you!

258
00:13:53,774 --> 00:13:55,214
Everything feels broken!

259
00:13:55,494 --> 00:13:58,731
Now that she's lost line of sight,
she'll stop firing on the castle,

260
00:13:58,814 --> 00:14:00,991
giving us a chance to
evacuate the capital?

261
00:14:01,074 --> 00:14:03,956
and leaving an opening to
launch a counterattack.

262
00:14:04,354 --> 00:14:06,754
It seems Mehpon can't fire continuously.

263
00:14:07,254 --> 00:14:10,571
There was a noticeable delay
between the first and second shots.

264
00:14:10,654 --> 00:14:13,151
I suspect that Vizd
attempting all that banter was

265
00:14:13,234 --> 00:14:15,091
her trying to keep us from
noticing its weakness.

266
00:14:15,174 --> 00:14:19,351
But thanks to that, we now know
Tachibana is being kept inside the robot.

267
00:14:19,434 --> 00:14:21,728
We can use this time to close in on it.

268
00:14:21,974 --> 00:14:24,111
My strength will return
if we get within range.

269
00:14:24,194 --> 00:14:26,312
And once my power's back, we attack.

270
00:14:26,614 --> 00:14:27,673
Got any questions?

271
00:14:27,934 --> 00:14:29,228
Just one little thing.

272
00:14:29,514 --> 00:14:32,131
Are you okay with me stealing
that got-me questions line?

273
00:14:32,214 --> 00:14:33,971
I want to add it to my
list of cool one-liners

274
00:14:34,054 --> 00:14:36,011
to use at some point
during my next adventure.

275
00:14:36,094 --> 00:14:37,251
There's no time for this.

276
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,687
The next shot's coming.

277
00:14:38,934 --> 00:14:39,854
Hey, Jinguji!

278
00:14:40,354 --> 00:14:42,589
I thought maybe a Crocodog would help.

279
00:14:49,234 --> 00:14:54,611
What the why am I
floating why even is this

280
00:14:54,694 --> 00:14:57,934
place where was I before I woke up here?

281
00:15:01,694 --> 00:15:04,151
They sure love their
giant laser beams in this

282
00:15:04,234 --> 00:15:08,134
world am I in the middle
of a battle right now?

283
00:15:12,974 --> 00:15:13,804
Jinguji.

284
00:15:20,254 --> 00:15:21,084
Nappan.

285
00:15:21,454 --> 00:15:22,284
Master?

286
00:15:24,194 --> 00:15:25,135
Tsukasa Jinguji.

287
00:15:25,334 --> 00:15:27,171
On behalf of myself and the school,

288
00:15:27,254 --> 00:15:30,851
I am happy to present you with this
award for your achievements in Kendo.

289
00:15:30,934 --> 00:15:32,169
Jinguji's so awesome!

290
00:15:32,374 --> 00:15:33,204
I can't even make the tea!

291
00:15:33,287 --> 00:15:35,431
I heard that he can pretty
much do anything he tries.

292
00:15:35,514 --> 00:15:37,161
Man, I wish I was that cool!

293
00:15:50,194 --> 00:15:51,774
This is so stupid!

294
00:15:52,014 --> 00:15:54,371
What idiot beat a sword that
can cut through life for me?

295
00:15:54,454 --> 00:15:56,411
These feelings be frustratingly effective.

296
00:15:56,494 --> 00:15:58,371
Do we have anything that can counter it?

297
00:15:58,454 --> 00:16:00,454
If I wasn't made for melee combat,

298
00:16:00,674 --> 00:16:02,991
if they close the gap, then
it's basically useless!

299
00:16:03,074 --> 00:16:06,051
Just hit him with whatever power
he used to break me out of jail!

300
00:16:06,134 --> 00:16:08,971
That spell takes more time
than we have to prepare.

301
00:16:09,054 --> 00:16:12,071
Can you do anything right now
besides being a loud mountain man?

302
00:16:12,154 --> 00:16:14,751
My skills are better suited
for covert operations.

303
00:16:14,834 --> 00:16:17,151
We need to figure out
something fast or we're hosed!

304
00:16:17,234 --> 00:16:19,031
If they're able to deflect my next attack,

305
00:16:19,114 --> 00:16:21,531
they'll be dead on top of me
and it's bye-bye Bunnybot!

306
00:16:21,614 --> 00:16:22,444
Right,

307
00:16:22,527 --> 00:16:25,851
to keep that from happening, I'll put every
ounce of power we have into this shop!

308
00:16:25,934 --> 00:16:28,431
You fool, that's not a
plan to search death!

309
00:16:28,514 --> 00:16:31,691
I can't get full power to set up a
reaction too big for man-pots to attack me!

310
00:16:31,774 --> 00:16:33,011
Shut up, I know what I'm doing!

311
00:16:33,094 --> 00:16:34,214
Now here I go!

312
00:16:36,914 --> 00:16:39,874
Uh, what happened? Is it
busted? What's going on?

313
00:16:40,054 --> 00:16:41,466
Is everything all right?

314
00:16:42,914 --> 00:16:43,744
The heck?

315
00:16:44,014 --> 00:16:45,771
Everything's shutting
down all of a sudden!

316
00:16:45,854 --> 00:16:48,454
Uh, shutting down? But how? What is this?

317
00:16:49,514 --> 00:16:50,632
We're almost there.

318
00:16:50,754 --> 00:16:52,771
We'll go under it and
attack from the other side.

319
00:16:52,854 --> 00:16:55,151
It won't be able to hit us with that beam.

320
00:16:55,234 --> 00:16:57,134
Look, Jinguji! Above us!

321
00:17:01,054 --> 00:17:05,172
At least you're smart enough to
change up your tactics at close range.

322
00:17:05,354 --> 00:17:08,231
But not smart enough to
take me on you rotten brat.

323
00:17:08,314 --> 00:17:10,074
Oh, sorry for being a brat

324
00:17:10,954 --> 00:17:12,794
Tachi bun is that you?

325
00:17:29,794 --> 00:17:33,954
I didn't mean I was referring to the hero!

326
00:17:35,914 --> 00:17:37,254
It's okay, Tachibana.

327
00:17:37,374 --> 00:17:38,609
I'm here to save you.

328
00:17:38,694 --> 00:17:40,251
You'll be safe in there for now.

329
00:17:40,334 --> 00:17:41,391
I'll get you out soon.

330
00:17:41,474 --> 00:17:42,994
Don't worry. Wow, okay.

331
00:17:43,274 --> 00:17:44,654
Why would I want out?

332
00:17:44,894 --> 00:17:47,271
I finally got my hands on some real power.

333
00:17:47,354 --> 00:17:48,411
Why should I give it up?

334
00:17:48,494 --> 00:17:50,431
Why go back to the way I was before?

335
00:17:50,514 --> 00:17:53,102
Is it me or is there
something off with him?

336
00:17:53,214 --> 00:17:54,743
You listen to me, Jinguuji.

337
00:17:55,634 --> 00:17:57,094
I will defeat you.

338
00:17:57,954 --> 00:17:58,784
Why?

339
00:17:58,867 --> 00:17:59,914
I came here to save you.

340
00:18:00,134 --> 00:18:02,171
Does it look like I need to be saved?

341
00:18:02,254 --> 00:18:07,354
Then again, you always have to be the hero,
reminding everyone how perfect you are.

342
00:18:08,034 --> 00:18:09,911
Women always adore you
even though you treat

343
00:18:09,994 --> 00:18:11,931
them like something that
crawled out of the sewer,

344
00:18:12,014 --> 00:18:14,471
and bosses love you because you're
perfect at everything you do!

345
00:18:14,554 --> 00:18:17,274
And that's why I friggin' hate you!

346
00:18:19,094 --> 00:18:21,574
Did you see that coming? I did not.

347
00:18:21,854 --> 00:18:23,431
You guys have a fight or something?

348
00:18:23,514 --> 00:18:24,344
No.

349
00:18:24,427 --> 00:18:25,871
I thought things were fine between us.

350
00:18:25,954 --> 00:18:26,784
Shut up, Jungle Jim!

351
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:28,151
You don't understand
what I've gone through!

352
00:18:28,234 --> 00:18:30,351
Maybe you're too perfect
to have repressed emotions,

353
00:18:30,434 --> 00:18:32,787
but I know I'm not for those both of us!

354
00:18:34,274 --> 00:18:38,511
I can feel this power flowing through me,
telling me to crush everything in my path.

355
00:18:38,594 --> 00:18:41,476
For the first time in my
life, I feel invincible!

356
00:18:41,574 --> 00:18:44,871
I didn't realize anyone still
used that kind of cheesy dialogue.

357
00:18:44,954 --> 00:18:47,971
I'm not sure Tachibana would
appreciate hearing that from you.

358
00:18:48,054 --> 00:18:49,391
This is getting out of hand.

359
00:18:49,474 --> 00:18:51,711
Why don't we just bust
in and break him loose?

360
00:18:51,794 --> 00:18:54,011
We're close enough now that your
strength should be back, right?

361
00:18:54,094 --> 00:18:55,574
Ah, about that.

362
00:18:55,934 --> 00:18:59,791
In spite of being closer, I'm afraid
my strength still hasn't returned.

363
00:18:59,874 --> 00:19:00,704
What?!

364
00:19:00,787 --> 00:19:02,151
You mean now I have to
fight this thing alone?!

365
00:19:02,234 --> 00:19:04,571
And how exactly do you expect
me to do that, genius?!

366
00:19:04,654 --> 00:19:09,595
All this time, I thought my strength was
tied directly to my proximity to Tachibana.

367
00:19:09,814 --> 00:19:12,171
The menu hasn't popped
up to explain anything.

368
00:19:12,254 --> 00:19:13,195
What's going on?

369
00:19:17,914 --> 00:19:19,326
Tachibana, listen to me!

370
00:19:20,194 --> 00:19:23,091
Sure, I'm popular with women and
bosses, but those are separate issues!

371
00:19:23,174 --> 00:19:25,251
Why are you only upset about it now?

372
00:19:25,334 --> 00:19:27,746
Probably because you say stuff like that.

373
00:19:28,354 --> 00:19:29,184
Why?

374
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:30,414
Oh, I'll tell you why.

375
00:19:32,514 --> 00:19:34,434
You never compliment me!

376
00:19:36,174 --> 00:19:37,004
Huh?

377
00:19:37,194 --> 00:19:38,914
You have no idea, do you?

378
00:19:39,074 --> 00:19:43,371
How people have treated me just for being
around you, let alone being your friend.

379
00:19:43,454 --> 00:19:46,336
Looking at me like a poo
trailing off a goldfish.

380
00:19:46,474 --> 00:19:51,062
That's barely the tip of the iceberg of
crappy opinions people have had of me.

381
00:19:51,554 --> 00:19:54,411
And you're not any better not one bit.

382
00:19:54,494 --> 00:19:57,451
Me we've been best
friends almost our entire

383
00:19:57,534 --> 00:20:00,351
lives and You've never
given me a compliment once.

384
00:20:00,434 --> 00:20:02,931
Even now I finally managed
to get stronger than you

385
00:20:03,014 --> 00:20:05,331
and you Still haven't done
anything nice about it.

386
00:20:05,414 --> 00:20:07,691
You need to do something quicker.

387
00:20:07,774 --> 00:20:08,604
He's gonna kill us.

388
00:20:08,687 --> 00:20:10,351
I don't know what to do.

389
00:20:10,434 --> 00:20:12,991
He told you straight up
that he wanted to be brave.

390
00:20:13,074 --> 00:20:14,371
So just give him a Compliment!

391
00:20:14,454 --> 00:20:15,711
Just give a compliment, huh?

392
00:20:15,794 --> 00:20:17,382
That should be easy, right?

393
00:20:19,374 --> 00:20:21,754
Hey, Tachibana! What? What is it?

394
00:20:22,514 --> 00:20:23,344
I think...

395
00:20:23,427 --> 00:20:25,174
you're super cool, bruh!

396
00:20:26,214 --> 00:20:28,391
You said that because you
feel like you have to!

397
00:20:28,474 --> 00:20:29,374
This is bad!

398
00:20:30,734 --> 00:20:31,564
Shikuchi!

399
00:20:37,034 --> 00:20:38,991
Since Japan has lots of earthquakes,

400
00:20:39,074 --> 00:20:41,291
Japanese doors are built to
take a lot of punishment.

401
00:20:41,374 --> 00:20:42,551
And look, not a scratch.

402
00:20:42,634 --> 00:20:45,311
I never would have thought
to use one like a shield.

403
00:20:45,394 --> 00:20:46,991
Now you've taken it too far.

404
00:20:47,074 --> 00:20:48,411
This isn't a game, Tachibana.

405
00:20:48,494 --> 00:20:49,371
This is dangerous.

406
00:20:49,454 --> 00:20:50,671
If I were anyone else, I'd be...

407
00:20:50,754 --> 00:20:52,551
Well, good thing you're not, huh?

408
00:20:52,634 --> 00:20:56,491
Everyone's always telling you how
amazing and cool you are, but not me.

409
00:20:56,574 --> 00:21:00,371
They sing your praises and never
say a single kind word about me.

410
00:21:00,454 --> 00:21:02,751
But you're the worst out of all of them.

411
00:21:02,834 --> 00:21:06,952
It's like you can't find a single
good thing about me, and that hurts.

412
00:21:07,494 --> 00:21:10,131
I just want a tenth of the
positive attention you get.

413
00:21:10,214 --> 00:21:13,171
I'm sorry you feel that way
and I'm trying to understand,

414
00:21:13,254 --> 00:21:15,491
but I can't do it when
you're throwing a tantrum!

415
00:21:15,574 --> 00:21:16,404
Shut up!

416
00:21:16,487 --> 00:21:17,891
Don't you think I know that already?

417
00:21:17,974 --> 00:21:20,739
I'd find some better way
to do this if I could.

418
00:21:21,094 --> 00:21:24,151
I understand that I'm being
childish and self-centered.

419
00:21:24,234 --> 00:21:26,334
And I realize it's not right.

420
00:21:26,694 --> 00:21:29,518
But sometimes I don't
know how to be a grown-up.

421
00:21:29,754 --> 00:21:30,694
I'm not smart.

422
00:21:30,894 --> 00:21:31,971
I'm not attractive.

423
00:21:32,054 --> 00:21:33,394
I always need saving.

424
00:21:33,674 --> 00:21:35,794
There's nothing special about me!

425
00:21:36,834 --> 00:21:38,194
He really is hurting.

426
00:21:41,114 --> 00:21:43,571
That's why they called me
a trailing goldfish poo!

427
00:21:43,654 --> 00:21:46,531
Because they knew I could
never be what you are, Jinguji!

428
00:21:46,614 --> 00:21:48,951
So no matter how much
cuter or stronger I get,

429
00:21:49,034 --> 00:21:52,152
if I'm worthless to you, it
means I truly am nothing!

430
00:21:52,254 --> 00:21:54,351
This is what it always comes back to!

431
00:21:54,434 --> 00:21:58,846
The only thing in my life I can brag
about is having you for a best friend!

432
00:22:00,794 --> 00:22:04,382
And I'm sick of being someone
who has something of their own!

433
00:22:11,314 --> 00:22:12,154
Fanta Fanta.

434
00:22:12,474 --> 00:22:13,794
To-mi-to-mi-to.

435
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:15,204
To-mi-to.

436
00:22:15,287 --> 00:22:16,454
Gang of desu. To-li-to.

437
00:22:16,674 --> 00:22:17,894
Ru-ru-ru.

438
00:22:22,214 --> 00:22:23,334
-

439
00:22:29,534 --> 00:22:30,364
Let's go.

440
00:22:35,394 --> 00:22:36,224
Yeah.

441
00:22:36,307 --> 00:22:39,791
Fanta Fanta Fanta Fanta And this
is a reality because it is true?

442
00:22:39,874 --> 00:22:40,815
I can't do this!

443
00:22:41,454 --> 00:22:43,711
Happiness happiness You won't fail to be!

444
00:22:43,794 --> 00:22:46,691
You won't fail to be!

445
00:22:46,774 --> 00:22:51,914
Kentucky code But here is
no one You can't partner

446
00:22:52,874 --> 00:22:56,274
You can't step up You want
to go I love you Yeah!

447
00:22:58,774 --> 00:23:06,171
I love you.

448
00:23:06,254 --> 00:23:07,084
Love like you.

449
00:23:07,167 --> 00:23:07,997
Love for love.

450
00:23:36,594 --> 00:23:38,074
I will now read a letter.

451
00:23:38,274 --> 00:23:40,991
I have a question about that freaky,
weird dog-crocodile creature.

452
00:23:41,074 --> 00:23:42,451
Oh, you mean the Crocodog?

453
00:23:42,534 --> 00:23:44,251
Do you know what kind of sound it makes?

454
00:23:44,334 --> 00:23:45,216
Let's find out!

455
00:23:45,374 --> 00:23:47,491
Come on, make a sound for the audience!

456
00:23:47,574 --> 00:23:48,994
Come on, speak, speak!
